<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="035" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-14: Add To Do carrying document and related record</title>
    <phase>3 Surfacing Spaarke</phase>
    <gate>013 complete (client document identity), 026 complete (related-record card)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF service code and `.tsx`; tags include bff-api and dataverse; writes production Dataverse rows with a fail-closed core-ancestor stamp. Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Adaptation of a shipped, working template (`CreateTodoAsync` + `CreateTodoView`) with the extension point named exactly. The one judgment boundary is covered by an explicit escalation trigger.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-c</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>013,026</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, frontend, fluent-ui, office-addin, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Let the user create a first-class `sprk_todo` from the task pane that carries **both** the open document and its related record as regarding. Reuse the shipped `POST /api/office/todo` endpoint and the existing `CreateTodoView` — this is an adaptation of working code, not a new surface. The current server-side regarding map covers Matter/Project/Invoice only; widen it to also set the document lookup.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in Dataverse polymorphic regarding (ADR-024), the `sprk_todo` entity model, and React + Fluent UI v9 inside an Office task pane. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>From the pane, in both Word and Outlook, the user creates a `sprk_todo` whose regarding carries the document **and** the related record. In Word that is the `sprk_document` plus the Matter/Project/Invoice; in Outlook it is the communication plus the record. The existing fail-closed core-ancestor stamp still holds. A contract test covers `POST /api/office/todo` with both regarding values, including the unauthorized negative case.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      **The working template, verified as-built.** `POST /api/office/todo` is declared at `Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:1178` and handled by `OfficeService.CreateTodoAsync:1499`. It already does everything except carry the document:

      - `_todoRegardingMap` at `:1490-1496` maps friendly names to `(lookupAttribute, logicalName)` — today only `Matter → sprk_regardingmatter`, `Project → sprk_regardingproject`, `Invoice → sprk_regardinginvoice`.
      - statecode 0 / statuscode 1 at `:1522-1523`; due date written as UTC-midnight from a `DateOnly` parse at `:1531-1536`; `sprk_assignedto` resolves to a **contact**, not a systemuser, at `:1545` (migrated 2026-06-21).
      - Regarding lookup plus the ADR-024 resolver fields `sprk_regardingrecordid` / `sprk_regardingrecordname` / `sprk_regardingrecordtype` at `:1553-1567`.
      - A **fail-closed** core-ancestor stamp: `_coreAncestors.StampAsync` at `:1574-1587` returns and the method yields `null` on failure, because creating the To Do without the stamp would be a silent inheritance hole.

      **The document lookup exists.** `sprk_todo` has a `sprk_regardingdocument` lookup to `sprk_document` — attested in the shared catalog at `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AssociateToStep/types.ts:112` and `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts:184`. So the widening is a map entry plus a request field, not a schema change.

      **The ADR-024 resolver fields are single-slot.** `sprk_regardingrecordid` / `-name` / `-type` can describe exactly ONE record. With two regarding values set (document + record), which one those denormalized fields describe is a real decision — see the escalation trigger.

      **The client side.** `CreateTodoView` is at `shared/taskpane/components/views/CreateTodoView.tsx`, wired in `App.tsx:240-280`, with the launcher at `shared/taskpane/services/createTodoLauncher.ts`.

      ⚠️ **The association-widening check (corrected as-built).** Design §9's warning about `UploadFinalizationWorker` widening now resolves to a single consolidated map: `Spaarke.Dataverse.DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` at `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:47`, which `UploadFinalizationWorker.ApplyAssociationLookup` calls. It **already handles** `sprk_workassignment` and `sprk_event`; `sprk_todo` is **deliberately absent** because `sprk_document` has no `sprk_todo` lookup column. `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:108`) carries the same deliberate omission with the same reason. That direction (document filed TO a to-do) does not exist and this task must not invent it — FR-14 goes the other way (to-do regarding a document), which `sprk_regardingdocument` supports.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/CreateTodoView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/createTodoLauncher.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/App.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AssociateToStep/types.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Client document identity — the resolved `sprk_document` GUID that becomes the To Do's document regarding.</dependency>
      <dependency task="026" status="pending">The related-to record card, which resolves which Matter/Project/Invoice the document is associated with and respects the two-slot association model.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: reuse `POST /api/office/todo` and `CreateTodoView`. Do NOT create a new endpoint, a new view, or a second To Do creation path. The change is a widened regarding map plus a widened request model plus client wiring.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The created To Do MUST carry BOTH regarding values when both exist: the document (`sprk_regardingdocument`) and the related record (`sprk_regardingmatter` / `sprk_regardingproject` / `sprk_regardinginvoice`). Setting only one when both are available is a defect, not a graceful degradation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">**Association-widening check (corrected):** the consolidated map is `Spaarke.Dataverse.DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:47`), mirrored by `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:108`). Both deliberately omit `sprk_todo` because `sprk_document` has no `sprk_todo` lookup column. This task MUST NOT add `sprk_todo` to either map — doing so would authorize a route whose upload can only ever land unassociated. If any part of this task appears to require filing a *document* to a to-do, that is the wrong direction: escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The fail-closed core-ancestor stamp at `OfficeService.cs:1574-1587` MUST remain fail-closed. If `StampAsync` fails, the To Do is NOT created. Do not soften it to a warning to make the two-regarding path succeed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">The denormalized resolver fields `sprk_regardingrecordid` / `sprk_regardingrecordname` / `sprk_regardingrecordtype` describe exactly one record. Whichever regarding value they describe MUST be chosen deliberately and documented in `notes/` — not left to whichever branch happens to run last.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">Every Dataverse GUID crossing a boundary in this task (documentId, regarding record id, assignee contact id, owner id) MUST be canonicalized to bare-lowercase via `cleanGuid`. Never interpolate a raw GUID into an OData key predicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">All To Do UI uses Fluent UI v9 and honors the Office light/dark theme via `useOfficeTheme`. No `Xrm`-bound components (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10">Shared-first: the Word/Outlook difference (document vs. communication as the non-record regarding) is expressed via `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()`, not `if (host === 'Word')` inside `CreateTodoView`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">`POST /api/office/todo` is modified, so its contract coverage MUST be extended to assert both regarding values are written, plus the unauthorized negative case. Banned: `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration assertions, ctor null-check assertions, `Stopwatch` + `Task.Delay`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">This task touches the BFF, so publish size MUST be measured **against a fresh build of `origin/master`, not the recorded baseline number** — worktree a detached `origin/master`, publish both, zip BOTH with PowerShell `Compress-Archive`, and report both absolute sizes, the delta and the tool. Ceiling 60 MB; escalate at ≥+5 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The PR MUST carry a **Placement Justification** section per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, and `/conflict-check` MUST be run before the BFF PR — `OfficeService.cs` is shared with `spaarkeai-compose-r8` and `unified-access-control-r2`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This task is in wave P3-c with 036 and 037. Do not modify `word/commands/**`, the Word manifest, or the share-link path — those belong to siblings in this wave.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Polymorphic regarding on `sprk_todo`; BFF-backed record ops from the Office pane</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/plan.md</file>
