      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-044-dataverse-guid-canonicalization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="polymorphic-resolver" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/polymorphic-resolver.md">Binding for the regarding lookup + denormalized resolver fields and for `cleanGuid` canonicalization.</pattern>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins — apply to the To Do form's density in the narrow pane.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md`, `spec.md` FR-14, `design.md` §9, and ADR-024. Read `OfficeService.CreateTodoAsync:1485-1600` in full before changing it. Emit the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL / sonnet / high). Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1">Verify against live Dataverse metadata that `sprk_todo.sprk_regardingdocument` exists and targets `sprk_document`. Record the confirmation.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide and record in `notes/035-todo-regarding-decision.md` which regarding value the single-slot ADR-024 resolver fields describe when both a document and a record are present. If the choice is not clear-cut, fire the escalation trigger instead of picking.</step>
    <step order="3">Widen `_todoRegardingMap` and the `CreateTodoRequest` model so the handler can accept and set both a document regarding and a record regarding in one call.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the two-regarding write in `CreateTodoAsync`, preserving statecode/statuscode, the UTC-midnight due-date semantics, the contact-typed `sprk_assignedto`, and — unchanged and still fail-closed — the core-ancestor stamp.</step>
    <step order="5">Wire the client: `CreateTodoView` and `createTodoLauncher` pass the resolved `sprk_document` (Word) or communication (Outlook) alongside the related record from task 026's card. Express the host difference through `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()`.</step>
    <step order="6">Extend `OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs` to assert both regarding values are written, the resolver fields describe the documented record, and the unauthorized negative case returns 401/403 with no row created.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm run typecheck` + `npm run build` in `src/client/office-addins` and `dotnet build` + `dotnet test`. Execute the `&lt;ui-tests&gt;` in both hosts.</step>
    <step order="8">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the ADR-029 constraint; record both absolute sizes, the delta and the tool.</step>
    <step order="9">Update `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If it is not clear which regarding value the single-slot ADR-024 resolver fields (`sprk_regardingrecordid` / `-name` / `-type`) should describe when both a document and a record are set, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Getting this wrong makes the To Do display under the wrong parent everywhere those denormalized fields are read.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the fail-closed core-ancestor stamp (`OfficeService.cs:1574-1587`) fails for the document-regarding path, STOP and escalate rather than softening it to a warning. A To Do created without the stamp is a silent access-inheritance hole.</trigger>
    <trigger>If completing this task appears to require adding `sprk_todo` to `DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` or `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType`, STOP and escalate — both omit it deliberately because `sprk_document` has no `sprk_todo` lookup column, and needing it means the data direction has been inverted.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Word — To Do carries document and record">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Spaarke-sourced Word document that is associated with a Matter.</step>
        <step>In the pane, create a To Do with a name and due date.</step>
        <step>Open the created `sprk_todo` in Dataverse.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>`sprk_regardingdocument` points at the open document's `sprk_document`, and `sprk_regardingmatter` points at the Matter. Both are set, not one.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Outlook — To Do carries communication and record">
      <steps>
        <step>In Outlook, select a message associated with a Matter and create a To Do from the pane.</step>
        <step>Open the created `sprk_todo`.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The communication regarding and the Matter regarding are both set, and the host difference came from `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()`, not a host-name conditional in the view.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Only a record available">
      <steps>
        <step>Create a To Do from the pane when the open document has no resolved `sprk_document` but a related record is known.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The To Do is created with the record regarding only, and the pane does not error or silently drop the create.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office host theme to dark and open the To Do form in the pane.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All fields, labels, the date picker and the submit/cancel controls use Fluent v9 theme tokens and remain legible with adequate contrast.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Keyboard navigation and announcement (NFR-11)">
      <steps>
        <step>Complete and submit the To Do form using the keyboard only.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every field and control is reachable with a visible focus ring; success and failure are announced via `useAnnounce`.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF: `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test`.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">`npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build` in `src/client/office-addins`.</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Confirm `sprk_todo.sprk_regardingdocument` metadata and inspect created rows.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/CreateTodoView.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/035-todo-regarding-decision.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Word document resolved to a `sprk_document` and associated with a Matter, when a To Do is created from the pane, then the created `sprk_todo` has BOTH `sprk_regardingdocument` and `sprk_regardingmatter` populated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an Outlook message associated with a record, when a To Do is created from the pane, then the created `sprk_todo` carries both the communication regarding and the record regarding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given both a document and a record regarding are set, when the row is written, then `sprk_regardingrecordid` / `-name` / `-type` describe the record documented in `notes/035-todo-regarding-decision.md` — consistently, not order-dependently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given only a record (no resolved document), when a To Do is created, then it is created with the record regarding only and no error is surfaced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `_coreAncestors.StampAsync` fails, when To Do creation runs, then NO `sprk_todo` row is created and the endpoint reports failure — the stamp remains fail-closed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unauthenticated or unauthorized caller, when `POST /api/office/todo` is called, then the response is 401/403 and no `sprk_todo` row is created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a request with an empty or whitespace-only name, when the endpoint is called, then it returns a validation failure and no row is created — not an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_todo` was NOT added to `DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` (`Models.cs:47`) or `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:108`) — verified by diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new endpoint and no second To Do view were created — verified by diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All five `&lt;ui-tests&gt;` pass, including the dark-mode and keyboard checks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean, `npm run build` succeeds, `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` are green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size was measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`; both absolute sizes, delta and tool are recorded; delta &lt;+5 MB and absolute &lt;60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-14 and the Owner Clarification "To Do only; defer Event". `design.md` §9 raised an association-widening concern against `UploadFinalizationWorker`; the as-built has since consolidated that logic into `DocumentAssociationMap.TryApply` (`Models.cs:47`), where `sprk_workassignment` and `sprk_event` are already handled and `sprk_todo` is deliberately excluded — the constraint above reflects the corrected location and the corrected conclusion. No `&lt;justification&gt;` block: this is an adaptation of the shipped `POST /api/office/todo` + `CreateTodoView`, not new surface.
  </notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
